          %title Contents
          %p
            This page is a result of the following question originally asked at
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric"}> Eric
              \: Is it true that given categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              that functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:C\to D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G:D\to C
              form an adjunction if the following diagram commutes for all morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:x\to y
              in
              = succeed "?" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mi G
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; y
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    G\circ F(y)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{G\circ F(f)}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    G\circ F(x)
                    }
            %p If so, is that an “if and only if” so that you can define adjunctions this way? If so, this would, in my opinion, be the most digestible way to define adjunctions for “scientists and engineers”.
          %h1#contents Contents
          .standout
            %p
              This page is an informal/speculative discussion of an alternative (yet hopefully equivalent) definition of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#attempt_2"} Attempt #2
              %ul
